# Show display names, never internal names

Anything a member can read — ticker entries, UI labels, modals, Discord messages,
tooltips, error text, exported guides — must use the **in-game display name**.
Internal identifiers are for code and logs only.

## Never render to a member

| Internal form | Example | Show instead |
|---|---|---|
| Entity class | `cds_combat_heavy_helmet_01_02_02` | `ADP-mk4 Helmet SecondWind` |
| Internal name | `behr_rifle_ballistic_01` | `P4-AR Rifle` |
| Localization key | `@item_Namebehr_rifle_ballistic_03_mr01` | `Behr Rifle Ballistic 03 MR01` |
| Debug name | `FoxwellEnforcement_Nyx_DefendShipNamed_M` | `Foxwell Enforcement Defend Ship Named M` |
| Pool key | `foxwellenforcement_ambush` | the mission's display title |
| UUID / contract id | `41231c57-f186-…` | the record's title |
| CIG placeholder | `~mission(Ship) Needs Assistance` | `Needs Assistance` |
| Raw JSON blob | `{"entityClass":"…","amount":1}` | `Wikelo Favor x50` |

## How to resolve

`scripts/lib/tickerLanguage.mjs` is the shared helper for script-side rendering:

- `buildDisplayNameResolver({ dataDir })` — entity class / internal name → display
  name, built from Wikelo trades, blueprints, components, weapons, mining and ordnance
- `cleanDisplayLabel(label, resolve)` — strips `@` keys, debug names and CIG placeholders
- `humanizeToken()` / `humanizeStatName()` — last-resort fallback for unknown ids
- `cleanGameText()` — removes `~mission(...)` style placeholders

In app code, prefer the display field already on the record (`displayName`,
`blueprintName`, `title`) and fall back to a resolver — never to the raw key.

## When no display name exists

CIG ships unlocalized items. Humanize the token (`behr_rifle_ballistic_03_mr01` →
`Behr Rifle Ballistic 03 MR01`); do **not** print the raw key or `@`-prefixed
localization key.

## Raw values are worse than no value

If a field cannot be phrased in plain language, **omit it**. Never dump JSON,
stat blobs, or internal field paths into member-facing text as filler.
